# ./gcdbench 4000037 1234567 131072  and  ./gcdbench 16000057 5000001 524288
# Sandbox: one core of a 2.1 GHz Xeon VM, NTL 11.5.1, distro gf2x 1.3.0 (untuned),
# machine otherwise idle.  Run before two row labels were renamed:
#   "(--ecg)"       is now "(--ecg-xgcd)"
#   "(--ecg-chain)" is now "(the default)"
gcd of a random residue with x^4000037 + x^1234567 + 1; NTL WITH gf2x; NTL finish below 131072 bits
  NTL GCD                           5.43 s   (gcd degree 0)
  CERTIFIED, NTL XGCD  (--ecg)      7.63 s    +40.6% vs NTL   [certified]
  hybrid HGCD, full apply (old)     7.08 s    +30.5% vs NTL
  hybrid HGCD, split apply          3.95 s    -27.2% vs NTL
  CERTIFIED, chain (--ecg-chain)    4.15 s    -23.5% vs NTL, +5.1% vs hybrid   [certified]
  all five agree: yes
gcd of a random residue with x^16000057 + x^5000001 + 1; NTL WITH gf2x; NTL finish below 524288 bits
  NTL GCD                          39.06 s   (gcd degree 0)
  CERTIFIED, NTL XGCD  (--ecg)     56.00 s    +43.4% vs NTL   [certified]
  hybrid HGCD, full apply (old)    55.02 s    +40.9% vs NTL
  hybrid HGCD, split apply         28.38 s    -27.3% vs NTL
  CERTIFIED, chain (--ecg-chain)   28.61 s    -26.7% vs NTL, +0.8% vs hybrid   [certified]
  all five agree: yes
